problem: polymorph spells operating on "stashes" are too convenient!!!

solution: give each affected item a slight chance of disintegrating.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
implementation A: attribute based
[disintegration factor, DF] = cTYPE + eLEV + IQ +LUCK

cTYPE = 0.000 for wizard, priest, healer
      = 0.000 for all else wearing ring of polymorph control
      = 0.017 for all else not wearing ring of polymorph control
eLEV = 0.001 * (30 - [exp.level])

IQ = 0.003 * (18 - [Intelligence])

LUCK = 0.0015 * (10 - [luck])  ... assumes a -10 to 10 scale.

under this scheme a samurai (for example) with Xp=13, In=12 and neutral
luck (0) would have DF = 0.067 and find that after casting 10 polymorph
spells onto the stash, half the stash would have disappeared!
------------------------------------------------------------------------
implementation B: greed based
DF = 0, if there are x or less items in the stash. let's say x = 10.
DF = 0.2 * [(n - x)/n] where n (>x) is the number of items in the stash.

under this scheme a stash would be whittled down to x items eventually.

you get the basic idea, polymorphing stashes should involve some kind
of risk.

